    "uz": "Applied to Uzbekistan without any Uzbek data, the naive splice jumps ×4.40 at 2012, the KZ-harmonized series ×1.77, a locally refitted one ×1.19 (MODIS alone ×1.37). In 2012–2019 the KZ model is off by 33.3% a month and -31.0% in total; the same model refitted on Uzbekistan: 16.0% and -0.3%. Uzbekistan's VIIRS/MODIS ratio is ×3.50, the KZ model implies ×2.42: VIIRS sees relatively more fires there (C1: small agricultural burns). 2025 contains the new industrial source near 38.1°N 67.3°E (C2), so the holdout is also shown to 2024 — it changes little.",
    "tm": "The naive splice jumps ×3.65 at 2012, the KZ-harmonized series ×1.42, a locally refitted one ×1.08 (MODIS alone ×1.21). Overlap error as-is 31.6% (bias -21.6%), local refit 18.9%. 57% of Turkmenistan's confident detections are static sources (Kazakhstan 13%); FIRMS `type` removes them in archive data and the mask in recent data (precision/recall above). The remaining error is the same kind as Uzbekistan's: VIIRS/MODIS ×3.20 vs ×2.50 from the KZ model. TM's monthly R is the lowest of the cell-level countries.",
    "annual": "Kyrgyzstan and Tajikistan have only a few hundred fire cell-days a year, so only annual totals are meaningful. KGZ: annual error 16.7%, bias -16.2% (raw MODIS: -71%); TJK: annual error 13.5%, bias +8.8% (raw MODIS: -73%). The harmonized totals are usable for a yearly trend, not for single months.",
    "transfer": "Transfers as-is: KAZ; does not: AUS, BRA, IND, KGZ, PRT, TJK, TKM, USA, UZB. The observed VIIRS/MODIS ratio ranges from ×1.54 to ×4.46; the KZ model cannot know a country's ratio and errs in the direction of the difference (too high for Portugal, too low for India). Refitted locally, the same model gets 5.2–41.7% monthly error. Honest conclusion: the METHOD transfers across biomes, the COEFFICIENTS do not — every country needs its own 2012–2019 overlap fit (which FIRMS provides everywhere).",
    "ba": "Holding burned area fixed, naive: continuous (95% CI includes 1) in none; KZ-harmonized: continuous (95% CI includes 1) in KAZ; locally harmonized: continuous (95% CI includes 1) in KAZ, TJK, TKM, UZB. The naive series jumps ×1.9–×4.0 everywhere. Correlation with burned area is high in Kazakhstan and weak in Kyrgyzstan/Tajikistan (few fires; much burned area there is not seen as active fire).",
